  {
    "id": "b33b0606520d524df6a3",
    "source": "A character at 0 HP is unconscious and dying or stable; GAME STATE shows their death-save track. The server tracks dying entirely: damage on a downed character adds automatic failures, healing any amount wakes them, and stabilize with the healerId of whoever tends them stops the dying without healing: it rolls that character's DC 10 Medicine check itself (or spends a healer's kit use with method \"kit\"), so never call request_roll for it first. In combat the server also rolls their death saves and announces the results. NEVER narrate a death or a recovery the tools have not reported, and never make death-save rolls yourself. A character GAME STATE marks DEAD comes back only through a revival spell cast with heal (spell and casterId: Revivify within a minute of the death, Raise Dead within ten days, Resurrection within a century, True Resurrection within two hundred years; the server checks the window and the material before it spends anything) or by the party lead; no other healing reaches them.",
    "sourceHash": "b33b0606520d524df6a31a53279521340639df8baa746ef6d38304b1570f1b88",
    "kinds": [
      "display-property"
    ],
    "sites": [
